---
title: Butternut Squash Mac and Cheese
portions: 6
category: Pasta
source: "https://www.lovingitvegan.com/vegan-mac-and-cheese/"
---

## Roast

[Preheat] Preheat the #oven{} to ^{200°C}.

[Toss] Add the @butternut-squash{600 g}(peeled, cubed) to a #mixing bowl{} with the @olive-oil{15 ml}, the @garlic{15 ml}(crushed), the @paprika{1 g}(smoked), the @salt{1 g}, the @black-pepper{0.5 g} and the @cayenne-pepper{0.5 g} and toss well.

[Roast] Spread evenly on a parchment-lined baking tray and roast until tender and roasted, ~{35 min}.

## Sauce

[Blend] While the squash roasts, add the @cashews{100 g}(raw), the @nutritional-yeast{12 g}, the @garlic-powder{2 g}, the @onion-powder{2 g}, the @dijon-mustard{15 ml}, the @lemon-juice{15 ml} and @vegetable-stock{240 ml}(1 cup) to a #blender{}. Blend until smooth.

[Finish sauce] When the squash is roasted, add it to the #blender{} with the remaining @vegetable-stock{240 ml} and blend until you have a smooth sauce.

## Serve

[Cook] Cook the @pasta{450 g}(macaroni) in salted boiling water in a large #pot{} and drain. ~{10 min}

[Toss] Return the pasta to the #pot{}, pour over the sauce and gently toss until well coated. Stir over low-medium heat to warm everything through, ~{3 min}.

[Serve] Top with chopped @parsley{} and ground @black-pepper{}.
